{#-
  The visible part of a batch's evidence comment on another batch's ticket. Handed its sources,
  it opens with one collapsed block summarised `Additional evidence from follow-up run
  <batch>.` holding them — the host, each basis entry, each draft with its source and
  transcript, and each witness — as ai-orchestrator's `render_comment` writes it (8bf72a30);
  without sources it opens with 0.5.0's line. Then the evidence, the bears-on paragraph and the
  question where `ticket comment` was handed them. onefollowup appends the comment's marker line
  after this; a template never writes it. Every variable README.md's "Templates" documents is
  given.
-#}
{%- if comment.sources -%}
{%- set metadata -%}
- Host: {{ comment.sources.host }}
{%- for origin, commit in comment.sources.basis | items %}
- Basis: {{ origin }} at {{ commit }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for draft in comment.sources.drafts %}
- Draft: {{ draft }}{% if comment.sources.draft_sources[draft] %}; {{ comment.sources.draft_sources[draft] }}{% endif %}{% if comment.sources.transcripts[draft] %}; transcript: {{ comment.sources.transcripts[draft] }}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for witness in comment.sources.witnesses %}
- Witness: {{ witness }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endset -%}
{{ collapsed("Additional evidence from follow-up run " ~ comment.batch ~ ".", metadata) }}
{%- else -%}
Additional evidence from follow-up run `{{ comment.batch }}`.
{%- endif %}

{{ comment.evidence | trim }}
{%- if comment.bears_on %}

Bears on the ticket: {{ comment.bears_on | trim }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if comment.question %}

{{ comment.question | trim }}
{%- endif %}
